    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/tests/suite/approvals.rs:323-358; codex-rs/core/tests/suite/request_permissions.rs:124-145",
      "finding": "All five fixtures emit exec_command JSON without shell or login. Approval helper naming shell_event still routes to exec_command."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/tests/common/test_codex.rs:158-179, 480-495, 1370-1394; codex-rs/core/tests/common/lib.rs:193-253",
      "finding": "These five use build(), which creates the implicit local environment. Default test builder disables ShellSnapshot and these fixtures never override it. Fresh Codex home is not an isolated OS login profile."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs:342, 3707; codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/unified_exec/exec_command.rs:237-247; codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/unified_exec.rs:101-137",
      "finding": "Default allow_login_shell is true. get_command maps an absent login argument to the selected environment allow_login_shell value."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/src/shell.rs:23-34; codex-rs/shell-command/src/shell_detect.rs:62-119, 266-289",
      "finding": "Bash/Sh/Zsh produce [shell, -lc, original cmd] when login is enabled. Unix shell selection uses getpwuid_r, followed by supported-shell fallback, not merely the SHELL environment variable."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/mod.rs:199-226; codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/unified_exec.rs:378-389",
      "finding": "No snapshot means the original command vector passes through unchanged; disabling ShellSnapshot does not disable login in tool commands."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/src/unified_exec/process_manager.rs:1234-1253; codex-rs/core/src/exec_env.rs:30-36; codex-rs/protocol/src/shell_environment.rs:54-58, 99-157",
      "finding": "The shell environment is constructed from the configured policy and parent environment. None of the five fixtures overrides shell environment variables or provides a controlled profile."
    },
    {
      "source": "evidence/host-profile-chain.json; evidence/native-r8b-fixture-runtime-audit.json",
      "finding": "Retained native host file bytes show /etc/profile sourcing im-config_wayland.sh, which sources initializer. initializer selects existing systemd-cat, sets initially empty IM_CONFIG_VERBOSE to the nonempty string false, and logger_debug tests nonemptiness. Two unconditional final calls plus a desktop-selection branch produce three logging calls in the already-audited empty-desktop case. The existing systemd-cat binary contains the exact error string."
    },
    {
      "source": "codex-rs/core/src/unified_exec/process_manager.rs:1114-1224; codex-rs/core/src/unified_exec/process.rs:371-391; both suite parse_result helpers",
      "finding": "The host-local/no-snapshot process path combines stdout and stderr into a single tool-output stream. The fixture field named stdout is aggregated output, so host startup stderr legitimately reaches the exact comparison; there is no separate descriptor API failure in these five blocks."
    }
